{"qid":"Q668","names":["Republic of India"],"title":"Republic of India","endonym":{"native":"भारत","lang":"hi"},"capsule":"The Republic of India came into being on 26 January 1950, when the Constitution of India replaced the Government of India Act and transformed the dominion (independent since 15 August 1947) into a sovereign democratic republic, with Rajendra Prasad as the first president. Under Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru (1947–1964) the country pursued non-alignment, industrialization under five-year plans, and the integration of over 500 princely states, while fighting wars with Pakistan (1947–1948, 1965, 1971) and China (1962). The 1971 war produced Bangladesh; the 1974 Pokhran nuclear test established India as a de facto nuclear power; and the post-1991 economic liberalization under Manmohan Singh set off sustained GDP growth that made India the world's fifth-largest economy by the early 21st century.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. National territory is defined by constitutional instruments; boundaries with Pakistan (including Kashmir) and China (Aksai Chin, Arunachal Pradesh) remain contested, introducing genuine geometric uncertainty in those sectors. Remaining frontiers are treaty-defined and well documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: India","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/India"},{"label":"Wikipedia: India","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India"}],"britannica":"place/India","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"India","rulers":[{"qid":"Q12446053","name":"Hari Singh I of Kashmir","start":1925,"end":1947,"image":"Sir Hari Singh Bahadur, Maharaja of Jammu and Kashmir, 1920.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sir%20Hari%20Singh%20Bahadur%2C%20Maharaja%20of%20Jammu%20and%20Kashmir%2C%201920.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Carl Vandyk","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"महाराजा हरि सिंह","nativeLang":"hi"},{"qid":"Q197736","name":"Rajendra Prasad","start":1950,"end":1962,"image":"Rajendra Prasad (Indian President), signed image for Walter Nash (NZ Prime Minister), 1958 (16017609534).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Rajendra%20Prasad%20(Indian%20President)%2C%20signed%20image%20for%20Walter%20Nash%20(NZ%20Prime%20Minister)%2C%201958%20(16017609534).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","artist":"Archives New Zealand from New Zealand","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"राजेन्द्र प्रसाद","nativeLang":"hi"},{"qid":"Q156349","name":"Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan","start":1962,"end":1967,"image":"Photograph of Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan presented to First Lady Jacqueline Kennedy in 1962.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Photograph%20of%20Sarvepalli%20Radhakrishnan%20presented%20to%20First%20Lady%20Jacqueline%20Kennedy%20in%201962.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"White House","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"सर्वपल्ली राधाकृष्णन","nativeLang":"hi"},{"qid":"Q144732","name":"Zakir Husain","start":1967,"end":1969,"image":"DR. ZAKIR HUSAIN - PICTORIAL BIOGRAPHY 0005.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/DR.%20ZAKIR%20HUSAIN%20-%20PICTORIAL%20BIOGRAPHY%200005.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Nation Museum Government of India","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"ज़ाकिर हुसैन","nativeLang":"hi"},{"qid":"Q312557","name":"V. V. Giri","start":1969,"end":1969,"image":"VV Giri 1974 stamp of India.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/VV%20G